cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "mhr-numerics: Numerical Mathematics Library for Arithmetic Spectroscopy"
version: "2.1"
date-released: "2026-03-01"
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.19165246
license: MIT
url: "https://github.com/TimakovGenesis/mhr-numerics"
repository-code: "https://github.com/TimakovGenesis/mhr-numerics"
abstract: >
  Companion code to the Arithmetic Spectroscopy paper series.
  Implements the variational MHR (Modular Hamiltonian Relaxation) operator
  framework for extracting arithmetic invariants of elliptic curves from
  spectral data, together with exact linear algebra over F_p and GF(2),
  lattice reduction, and polynomial interpolation.
authors:
  - family-names: Timakov
    given-names: Andrew
    email: andrew.genesis@proton.me
keywords:
  - elliptic curves
  - arithmetic spectroscopy
  - MHR operator
  - spectral gap
  - BSD conjecture
  - variational methods
  - lattice reduction
  - finite fields
references:
